  The scalars-only network matches the kNN posterior, confirming the network
  does learn the correct scalar posterior. So it is a clean control.

  The full model is 28% tighter than the scalars-only ablation.
  That gap cannot come from the period prior (both models have it) and cannot
  come from the four scalars (both models see them). It can ONLY come from the
  light curve - the CNN is reading transit shape, most plausibly impact
  parameter via the ingress slope and the V-vs-U profile.

